.TH WACOM-STEER 1 "October 2026" "wacom-steer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wacom-steer \- Wacom stylus steering and analog gamepad input bridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wacom-steer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wacom-steer
is a lightweight, userspace input bridge for Linux that maps Wacom stylus coordinates into analog gamepad controls (steering, throttle, brake) via Linux \fB/dev/uinput\fR.
.PP
Unlike standard stylus tools, \fBwacom-steer\fR opens source event devices in passive non-exclusive mode (without \fBEVIOCGRAB\fR), allowing the stylus to continue tracking the host desktop cursor normally.
The virtual gamepad is configured as a standard Microsoft USB gamepad (Vendor ID 0x045e, Product ID 0x028e), enabling seamless recognition by Steam, Wine, Proton, and native Linux games through SDL2 and evdev.
.SH MODES OF OPERATION
.TP
.B Joystick Mode (Default)
In joystick mode (\fB\-\-mode joystick\fR), the tablet emulates an analog Xbox 360 gamepad controller:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Stylus X-axis maps to steering/yaw in either \fBabsolute\fR (direct 1:1 wheel angle) or \fBrelative\fR (rate-based deflection with auto-centering return spring) mode.
.IP \(bu 2
Stylus Y-axis maps to accelerator and brake pedals (\fB\-\-pedal\-mode split\fR or \fB\-\-pedal\-mode combined\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Stylus switches and tablet ExpressKeys map to dynamic recentering and gamepad buttons.
.IP \(bu 2
Operates passively without \fBEVIOCGRAB\fR, preserving normal desktop cursor tracking.
.RE
.TP
.B Mouse Mode
In relative mouse mode (\fB\-\-mode mouse\fR or \fB\-\-mouse\fR), the tablet emulates a virtual relative mouse (\fIWacom Steer Virtual Mouse\fR):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Designed for 3D camera aiming (such as Minecraft or first-person shooters) and relative trackpad navigation.
.IP \(bu 2
Acquires exclusive device grab (\fBEVIOCGRAB\fR) so raw absolute tablet events do not leak to the compositor or XWayland, eliminating camera spinning.
.IP \(bu 2
Supports \fBdelta\fR style (natural trackpad swipe with baseline resets on pen lift) and \fBrate\fR style (joystick deflection rate with resting deadzone).
.RE
.TP
.B Pedal Mode
In dedicated pedal mode (\fB\-\-mode pedal\fR or \fB\-\-pedal\fR), the tablet acts exclusively as an analog throttle and brake unit:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Horizontal steering is locked to neutral center (0).
.IP \(bu 2
Stylus Y-axis maps directly to analog triggers (\fBABS_RZ\fR throttle, \fBABS_Z\fR brake) or combined stick axis (\fBABS_Y\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Ideal for using the tablet alongside a physical steering wheel, flight stick, or keyboard.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to custom TOML configuration file. If omitted, defaults to \fI~/.config/wacom-steer/config.toml\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " PATH"
Explicit path to an input event device node (e.g. \fI/dev/input/event7\fR). Bypasses automatic device scoring and selection.
.TP
.BI \-\-device\-name " TEXT"
Substring to match against device names during automatic scanning (default: "Wacom").
.TP
.BI \-\-vendor " HEX"
USB vendor ID in hex format (e.g. \fI056a\fR for Wacom).
.TP
.BI \-\-product " HEX"
USB product ID in hex format (e.g. \fI0375\fR for Intuos M).
.TP
.BI \-\-center " F"
Normalized tablet horizontal center position in the range [0.0..1.0] (default: 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-half\-span " F"
Distance from center required to reach full steering lock, in normalized coordinates (0.0..1.0] (default: 0.5). Narrower values allow full lock with smaller hand motions.
.TP
.BI \-\-deadzone " F"
Deadzone around neutral steering center in the range [0.0..1.0) (default: 0.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-curve " F"
Exponential power curve factor for steering (> 0.0, default: 1.0). Values greater than 1.0 provide finer sensitivity around center with faster ramp towards full lock.
.TP
.B \-\-invert
Inverts the steering direction (left becomes right, right becomes left).
.TP
.BI \-\-steering\-mode " absolute|relative"
Selects the steering mode: \fBabsolute\fR (default) or \fBrelative\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-relative\-turn\-rate " F"
Turn rate in full-lock sweeps per second at 100% deflection in relative mode (default: 2.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-relative\-return\-rate " F"
Auto-centering return speed in full sweeps per second when in resting deadzone (default: 3.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-relative\-deadzone " F"
Resting deadzone around center in relative mode where auto-centering engages (default: 0.05).
.TP
.BI \-\-recenter\-button " NAME|HEX"
Button to use for dynamic on-the-fly recentering. Supports stylus switches (\fIbtn_stylus\fR, \fIbtn_stylus2\fR), ExpressKeys (\fIbtn_0\fR..\fIbtn_9\fR), and hex codes (\fI0x14b\fR). Set to \fInone\fR to disable (default: none).
.TP
.BI \-\-pedal\-mode " off|split|combined"
Pedal mapping mode for stylus vertical Y-axis: \fBoff\fR (default), \fBsplit\fR (analog triggers ABS_Z/ABS_RZ), or \fBcombined\fR (ABS_Y stick axis).
.TP
.BI \-\-pedal\-center " F"
Normalized neutral center position for pedals along the vertical axis [0.0..1.0] (default: 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-pedal\-half\-span " F"
Normalized travel from pedal center to reach 100% throttle or brake (default: 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-pedal\-deadzone " F"
Neutral coasting deadzone band around pedal center [0.0..1.0) (default: 0.05).
.TP
.BI \-\-pedal\-curve " F"
Exponential response curve factor for pedals (> 0.0, default: 1.0).
.TP
.B \-\-pedal\-invert
Inverts pedal direction (forward becomes brake, backward becomes throttle).
.TP
.BI \-\-lift " center|hold"
Pen proximity behavior when stylus leaves the tablet surface. \fBcenter\fR (default) immediately zeroes steering and pedals for safety; \fBhold\fR maintains the last active values.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " joystick|mouse|pedal"
Select operating mode: \fBjoystick\fR (analog steering and optional pedals, default), \fBmouse\fR (relative mouse aiming), or \fBpedal\fR (dedicated accelerator and brake pedals with locked steering).
.TP
.B \-\-mouse
Shorthand flag to enable relative mouse camera mode (alias: \fB\-\-minecraft\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-pedal
Shorthand flag to enable dedicated pedal mode.
.TP
.B \-\-joystick
Shorthand flag to enable analog joystick/gamepad mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-mouse\-style " delta|rate"
Aiming style in mouse mode: \fBdelta\fR (trackpad swipe, default) or \fBrate\fR (joystick deflection rate) (alias: \fB\-\-minecraft\-style\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-mouse\-sensitivity " F"
Aiming sensitivity multiplier for mouse mode (> 0.0, default: 1.0) (alias: \fB\-\-minecraft\-sensitivity\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-mouse\-deadzone " F"
Resting deadzone around center for mouse rate mode in [0.0..1.0) (default: 0.05) (alias: \fB\-\-minecraft\-deadzone\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-mouse\-invert\-y
Inverts vertical pitch in mouse mode (moving pen up looks down) (alias: \fB\-\-minecraft\-invert\-y\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " trace|debug|info|warn|error"
Logging verbosity level (default: info).
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " SHELL"
Generate shell tab completion script and exit. Supported shells: \fBzsh\fR, \fBbash\fR, \fBfish\fR, \fBelvish\fR, \fBpowershell\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Outputs this manual page to standard output and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Probe mode: scans and prints hardware diagnostics, axis limits, and active configuration without creating a virtual uinput device.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Prints effective merged configuration as formatted TOML to standard output and exits.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Displays brief help information.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Displays version information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wacom-steer/config.toml
Default user configuration file.
.TP
.I /dev/uinput
Linux userspace input subsystem character device used to create virtual gamepads and mice.
.TP
.I /dev/input/event*
Kernel evdev interface device nodes for tablets and stylus input.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run in default analog joystick mode with automatic hardware detection:
.B wacom-steer
.TP
Run diagnostic probe to inspect connected devices without creating virtual devices:
.B wacom-steer \-\-dry\-run
.TP
Run in relative mouse mode for 3D camera aiming (e.g. Minecraft):
.B wacom-steer \-\-mouse
.TP
Run in dedicated pedal mode (throttle and brake on stylus Y-axis, steering centered):
.B wacom-steer \-\-pedal
.TP
Enable dual-trigger pedals on stylus vertical axis with 8% deadzone in joystick mode:
.B wacom-steer \-\-pedal\-mode split \-\-pedal\-deadzone 0.08
.TP
Enable relative steering mode with dynamic recentering on the lower stylus barrel switch:
.B wacom-steer \-\-steering\-mode relative \-\-recenter\-button btn_stylus
.TP
Narrow active steering width to 35% of tablet width for sharper turns:
.B wacom-steer \-\-half\-span 0.35
.TP
Generate and source zsh completion dynamically:
.B source <(wacom-steer \-\-completions zsh)
.TP
View manual page directly in terminal:
.B wacom-steer \-\-man | man \-l \-
